[5]  THE SHUFFLE CONTROL.  Degree-preserving permutation of which links belong to which
     plaquettes.  Scored TWO ways, because the two ways answer different questions.
       (i)  against the ORIGINAL carrier's adjacency -- does the method just replay a fixed
            answer that the counts or the labels already fix?   Must COLLAPSE.
       (ii) against the SHUFFLED carrier's OWN adjacency -- does the method track the
            carrier it is actually run on?   Must HOLD.

